# Wave W17-AB (Route 223): league sand — deep-lane sand, cliff-shadow flecks: a dark slate-teal sand lying under deep water on the League run, carrying cliff-shadow flecks where the Summit cliff throws its shade down the lane and sparse pale shell glints where the light still reaches (design: the League sea road — all water, north to the Summit Road shore; the cliff at the end of it has heard every promise trainers make). Route 223’s own sand — split from the south sea’s bright and long sands by depth entire (dark deep-lane bottom vs gold shallows and sparse open-sea pale) and from its twin Route 229’s loop sand ahead of the program by shade: this sand lies in a cliff’s shadow, that one in open offshore light.
